triage:C5_QA1_REQ_C5_001 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C5-001" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "fixed" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f7d58b1c8556b55fcff744cfa3e3c5775521b795" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/src/lib.rs:96; tests/integration/cron-consumer/tests/execution.rs:2" ;
 triage:issue "The public sc_cron::observability module is absent at the reviewed head. The committed isolated execution consumer imports it and does not compile (E0432 in /tmp/c5-consumer-facade-blocked.log). Actual Rust/Python/Monty/custom-host and attached/launched/finished receiver acceptance therefore remains unproved. Separate PR115 source is not part of PR118." ;
 triage:action "Consume the qualified public facade, reconcile its exact exported names with the frozen compatibility contract, and execute both default and explicit Monty isolated consumer suites plus normal graph guard at the resulting source. Do not introduce another trait or direct sc-command consumer dependency." ;
 triage:fix_disposition "Canonical nominal facade consumed; isolated Rust/Python and Monty custom-host execution plus bounded normal graph guards." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6647574110" .

triage:C5_QA1_REQ_C5_002 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C5-002" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "fixed" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f7d58b1c8556b55fcff744cfa3e3c5775521b795" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/src/operation.rs:127; crates/sc-cron/src/scheduler/consumer.rs:161" ;
 triage:issue "request_stop is synchronous and independent, but Controller::stop silently omits all future G/K timer notifications when called from a normal thread without an entered Tokio handle. With native COMMIT held after admission, a stop issued from that thread records future G/K and Draining but cannot publish DeadlineExceeded at grace independently of physical completion/join: try_current returns Err and the sole timer is never spawned. Cooperative checks do not repair the held native interval." ;
 triage:action "Own timer/notification execution on the worker lifecycle runtime (or an equivalent retained independent owner), rather than the calling thread ambient runtime. Add a causal regression issuing request_stop from an ordinary std thread while admitted native work is held, proving grace status before release/join and second-stop shortening without extending K." ;
 triage:fix_disposition "Retained owning runtime schedules stop expiry independently of ordinary caller thread; held admitted native COMMIT regression and original-behavior negative." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6647574110" .

triage:C5_QA1_REQ_C5_003 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C5-003" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "fixed" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f7d58b1c8556b55fcff744cfa3e3c5775521b795" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/tests/hook_environment/owned_child.rs:17; crates/sc-cron/src/sqlite_cooperative_tests.rs:39; crates/sc-cron/src/sqlite_cooperative_tests.rs:81; tests/integration/cron-consumer/tests/execution.rs:89; tests/integration/cron-consumer/tests/application_schema.rs:120" ;
 triage:issue "The Windows helper is repaired, but its non-Windows Drop still calls an unbounded wait. New proof fixtures also contain readiness waits outside failure guards and do not consistently retain physical joins on assertion failure: hold uses entered.recv(), most callers retain raw holder JoinHandles instead of the HeldConnection guard, the external execution test waits unbounded for ManualClock readiness, and the forwarding-provider test drops its physical JoinHandle if a preceding assertion fails. The new explicit no-hang/no-race ownership policy is not yet satisfied." ;
 triage:action "Complete the shared Unix ownership redesign; bound readiness as failure detection, retain cancellation/release and physical joins through every assertion/error path, and use causal negative witnesses that intentionally fail each handshake/cleanup stage. Reuse the proven ownership helper where suitable; no retry, skip, serialization, or timeout padding." ;
 triage:fix_disposition "Canonical Unix/Windows process owners consumed; all C5 SQLite and isolated fixtures supervised, release guards retain bounded physical joins; ignored-cancellation assertion unwind witness. Unix bridge now requires canonical inspection before dispatch; missing-inspector real-entry regression fails original behavior." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6647574110" .

triage:C5_QA1_REQ_C5_004 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C5-004" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "fixed" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f7d58b1c8556b55fcff744cfa3e3c5775521b795" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/src/scheduler/consumer.rs:102; crates/sc-cron/src/scheduler/consumer.rs:111; crates/sc-cron/src/scheduler.rs:603" ;
 triage:issue "The new Result-returning spawn_worker_cooperative delegates to spawn_worker_mode, whose duplicate-worker compare_exchange failure asserts. Calling the cooperative method twice while the first worker is alive panics instead of returning CronError. The legacy public spawn_worker documentation does not waive the active no-public-panic requirement for this new fallible API." ;
 triage:action "Claim cooperative worker ownership through a fallible internal path and return a fixed typed CronError for an already-running worker; preserve the legacy signature separately if compatibility requires it. Add a deterministic second-call refusal test and verify the original worker remains usable and physically joined." ;
 triage:fix_disposition "Fallible runtime validation and atomic worker claim return fixed typed startup errors; duplicate/no-runtime regressions fail original behavior and preserve original worker ownership." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6647574110" .

