triage:C5_QA1_ARCH_C5_002 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "ARCH-C5-002" ;
 triage:severity "BLOCKING" ;
 triage:reviewer "arch-qa" ;
 triage:status "fixed" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f7d58b1c8556b55fcff744cfa3e3c5775521b795" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/src/operation.rs" ;
 triage:issue "Independent expiry ownership is conditional on the request_stop caller having an entered Tokio runtime. A public stop request from an ordinary synchronous thread records a future budget but skips the only future expiry-notification task. With a blocked native provider and no join, live cutoffs may be checked later but G/K status and interrupts are not independently scheduled. This violates the approved owned shutdown/typed expiry architecture; the stop API documents no caller-runtime precondition." ;
 triage:action "Capture/use the owning runtime or another lifecycle-owned notification mechanism independently of caller thread context. Prove an ordinary-thread stop while physical work is held publishes expiry without waiting for join; retain cancellation and notifier ownership." ;
 triage:fix_disposition "Retained owning runtime schedules stop expiry independently of ordinary caller thread; held admitted native COMMIT regression and original-behavior negative." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6647574110" .

