 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6647574110" .

triage:C5_QA1_ARCH_C5_004 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "ARCH-C5-004" ;
 triage:severity "BLOCKING" ;
 triage:reviewer "arch-qa" ;
 triage:status "fixed" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f7d58b1c8556b55fcff744cfa3e3c5775521b795" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/tests/hook_environment/owned_child.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The Unix test owner destructor calls ChildWrapper::wait without a bound after start_kill. A failed handshake or timeout therefore enters an unbounded cleanup wait instead of a failure path that retains and reclaims the whole process tree. The new project Validation Policy expressly prohibits this test design. Passing child-run deadlines do not bound its destructor." ;
 triage:action "Use an owned whole-session cleanup design with causal readiness and actual physical completion on success and failure. Bound and report failed cleanup honestly; no sleep/padding/retry or leader-only substitute." ;
 triage:fix_disposition "Canonical Unix/Windows process owners consumed; all C5 SQLite and isolated fixtures supervised, release guards retain bounded physical joins; ignored-cancellation assertion unwind witness. Unix bridge now requires canonical inspection before dispatch; missing-inspector real-entry regression fails original behavior." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6647574110" .

