triage:C5_QA1_FTQ_C5_001 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C5-001" ;
 triage:severity "critical" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "fixed" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f7d58b1c8556b55fcff744cfa3e3c5775521b795" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/tests/hook_environment/owned_child.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The Unix destructor sends start_kill, discards any error, then calls ChildWrapper::wait without a deadline. When termination or wrapper completion does not occur, the test hangs during normal cleanup or assertion unwinding despite output() having an execution deadline. The outer execution timeout does not bound this destructor." ;
 triage:action "Consume the actual bounded Unix owner redesign from the shared parent, preserving raw OS arguments and whole-session physical cleanup. Prove timeout, panic, failed handshake and descendant cleanup through the real entry point. Do not add a larger test timeout or merely poll the leader." ;
 triage:fix_disposition "Canonical Unix/Windows process owners consumed; all C5 SQLite and isolated fixtures supervised, release guards retain bounded physical joins; ignored-cancellation assertion unwind witness. Unix bridge now requires canonical inspection before dispatch; missing-inspector real-entry regression fails original behavior." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6647574110" .

triage:C5_QA1_FTQ_C5_002 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C5-002" ;
 triage:severity "critical" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "fixed" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f7d58b1c8556b55fcff744cfa3e3c5775521b795" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/tests/hook_environment/owned_child_windows.rs" ;
 triage:issue "Cleanup returns success as soon as the std leader is reaped and job membership is empty. That is not the same boundary as all descendant process identity handles being signaled. The witness immediately queries retained identity handles, so job-list removal preceding the process-signaled observation makes the same correct test intermittently fail and makes the owner falsely claim physical completion." ;
 triage:action "Consume the shared retained-process-identity completion redesign. Success must require leader reaping, genuine empty membership and completion signals for the owned process identities. Keep the original cleanup deadline and immediate witness; add/retain a deterministic empty-job-before-unsignaled-handle negative. Do not compensate with an observer delay, retries or deadline padding." ;
 triage:fix_disposition "Shared Windows owners require empty membership plus signaled retained identities; Python-only supervisor fixed equivalently, native Windows applicable suite passed and deterministic unsignaled-identity negative retained." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6647574110" .

triage:C5_QA1_FTQ_C5_003 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C5-003" ;
 triage:severity "critical" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "fixed" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f7d58b1c8556b55fcff744cfa3e3c5775521b795" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/src/sqlite_cooperative_tests.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The cancellation regression holds the real connection mutex in one thread, requests stop, then performs an unbounded physical.join before releasing that mutex. If a store path stops observing cancellation, the operation waits for the mutex while the test waits for its join, and release.send at521 is unreachable. This is a deterministic hang in exactly the regression the test is meant to report. Other new fixtures also await joins or drop raw JoinHandles on assertion failure without a bounded owning test envelope." ;
 triage:action "Redesign the deadlock-sensitive acceptance fixtures with explicit handshake/release ownership and a bounded supervisor that can reclaim the entire test process if native work cannot complete. Ensure every failure and unwinding path releases barriers, cancels work and physically reaps it. Do not rely on unbounded Drop joins or a Tokio timeout that leaves blocking work behind. Cover the ignored-cancellation and failed-assertion paths causally." ;
 triage:fix_disposition "Canonical Unix/Windows process owners consumed; all C5 SQLite and isolated fixtures supervised, release guards retain bounded physical joins; ignored-cancellation assertion unwind witness. Unix bridge now requires canonical inspection before dispatch; missing-inspector real-entry regression fails original behavior." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6647574110" .

triage:C5_QA1_FTQ_C5_004 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C5-004" ;
 triage:severity "critical" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "fixed" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "f7d58b1c8556b55fcff744cfa3e3c5775521b795" ;
 triage:file "tests/integration/cron-consumer/graph_guard.py" ;
 triage:issue "Both Cargo invocations use subprocess.run with captured pipes and neither an execution deadline nor process-tree ownership. A Cargo process waiting indefinitely for another live Cargo owner/file lock stalls the acceptance gate; a descendant retaining a captured pipe can also keep collection open. --offline prevents network resolution, not these waits." ;
 triage:action "Run the graph checks through the existing bounded owned-process supervisor with isolated per-run paths as appropriate, regular-file output capture and whole-tree cleanup on all failures. Apply the same rule to any retained qualification probes; temporary probes can instead be removed under the existing closeout requirement. Add a causal stalled-tool/descendant-held-output negative using the existing helper tests, not timeout padding." ;
 triage:fix_disposition "Graph checks reuse bounded canonical Python process owner with regular-file capture and whole-tree cleanup; existing stalled-descendant failure/timeout witnesses retained, Windows identity completion repaired." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/118#issuecomment-6647574110" .
